# Original Palette, Readable Lettering and Publication

Status: DONE
Milestone: M4 First public GitHub Pages release complete
Dependencies: 06_TESTING_AND_LAUNCH.todo, 09_STORY_AND_CAKE_STICKERS.todo, 10_CUTE_CURSIVE_DESIGN.todo

## Purpose

Restore the user's original colours, replace overly elaborate cursive with
clearer handwriting, keep the liked design details and publish the requested page.

## Tasks

- [x] Archive the prior palette/font revision without changing original cake files.
- [x] Restore cream #f5ebdd, deep green #34483a and restrained terracotta.
- [x] Use locally hosted, SIL-licensed Courgette in place of Dancing Script.
- [x] Preserve story, stickers, cute details and readable DM Sans instructions.
- [x] Update the sharing image and set the real GitHub Pages base URL.
- [x] Review locally, including actual palette/font loading and enlarged text.
- [x] Stage only site/, .gitignore and the Pages workflow.
- [x] Commit with co-author trailer and push using existing normal Git credentials.
- [x] Wait for the deployment and review the actual public page.
- [x] Preserve private sources and distinguish publication from final design acceptance.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The original palette is present in real computed browser styles.
- [x] Courgette loads; body/actions remain legible and primary controls at least 48px.
- [x] Four sections, all five real cakes, full-photo links and direct contact remain.
- [x] Local/public browser reviews pass, including 200% text on phones and desktop.
- [x] Public output contains 58 allowlisted files, not private archives or masks.
- [x] Actions reports success for the exact pushed commit.
- [x] The live page and key assets match release bytes.
- [x] Unverified native-app/user acceptance and hosting-policy risk remain explicit.

